description: Use the ai-maestro-visual-communicator-plugin to generate browser-ready technical diagrams and review pages
globs: **/*
alwaysApply: false
---

Use the canonical `amvcp-visual-communication` skill at `skills/amvcp-visual-communication/` in the repo. Cursor support is rules-based guidance, not native Agent Skills support.

When the user asks for a diagram, architecture overview, diff review, plan review, project recap, slide deck, or complex comparison table, read `skills/amvcp-visual-communication/SKILL.md` and follow its workflow. Use the command markdown in `commands/amvcp-*.md` as templates when helpful.

Write generated HTML to `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_ROOT/reports/visual-communicator/diagrams/` unless the user asks for another path, then open it in a browser if Cursor permits shell/browser access. If browser access is blocked, report the file path.

Command palettes may not expose these `/amvcp-*` templates directly in Cursor. `/amvcp-share-page` requires the Pi-compatible `vercel-deploy` script, so treat sharing as optional and environment-dependent.
